Except that they are not artifacts, nor are they named items. Becides the 
fact that there can only be one of them, there isn't much that makes the 
unique items similar to artifacts. Artifacts are a layer added on top of 
a base item, (Frostbrand is a longsword, The Sceptre of Might is a mace). 
The invocation items are unique base items on there own (The bell of 
opening is the only silver bell, the Book Dead is the only papyrus 
spellbook, etc). The quick way to confirm that they arn't artifacts 
without looking at the source is to use the \ command. The unique items 
fall under a different heading then the artifacts, and they also appear 
under their general catagories. If you have Frost Brand ided, you won't 
see "Frost Brand [unaligned long sword] under weapons, but if you have 
the Bell of Opening you will see "Bell of Opening (Silver Bell)" under 
tools. There is also the fact that the unique items can't be put into 
containers, while artifacts can be.

